# Generated data files.
#
# These are rewritten wholesale by the scheduled workflows -- there is no such
# thing as a meaningful line-level merge of a .parquet or .xlsx. Git normally
# guesses "binary" by looking for NUL bytes in the first 8KB, which is a guess
# it can get wrong; when it guesses wrong it will happily run a TEXT merge and
# write conflict markers into the middle of a data file, producing something
# that still loads as a file but is corrupt.
#
# Marking them explicitly means a collision is always an honest conflict rather
# than a silently mangled file. The workflows resolve that conflict by keeping
# the run's freshly pulled data (see the `-X theirs` in each commit step).
*.parquet binary
*.xlsx    binary
*.xlsm    binary
